Storm Lord Cahalith, despite the fact we can create a thousand different profiles, unify the Iminir stoicism, tactical and cold attitude, to the Gibbous Moon monstrosity.<br /> It is a cold, frostibitten horror of an apex predator, ready to chill your bones and your blood with pure fear.</div> </div> </div> </div>I gotta say, you really managed to show me how awesome a Cahalith can be! It really embodies the image that I thing can be one of the best in a horror scene: the prey feeling each time more and more hopeless in the face of a predator that is not only after it, but is savoring the situation and taking his sweet time in the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-29T23:56:12-07:00","id":1534932,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1534479-compatibility-between-1ed-and-2ed?p=1534924#post1534924\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see. So in a crossover chronicle I could in theory have an Iminir and a Bound in the same group, evem friends, but in that case the Uratha would be more of an exception, right?I could see it being the hook for a story with other werewolves as enemies hunting the Geist...</div> </div> </div> </div>Local variance is the name of the game when it comes to integrating different supernatural creatures into the same group, so yes, it's theoretically doable; various other gamelines amply demonstrate how the uneven distribution of trust and incomplete information between groups and individuals can see lines drawn in the sand when it comes to siding with your friends or your peers in the face of unfamiliar supernatural quantities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Which brings me another question: can a Siskur-Dah be called off? Or would that end up being a kill or be killed situation? </div> </div> </div>The hunt goes until it stops, one way or another, as described in the Siskur-Dah Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-01T22:17:35-07:00","id":1535050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1534479-compatibility-between-1ed-and-2ed?p=1534932#post1534932\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The hunt goes until it stops, one way or another, as described in the Siskur-Dah Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what about the lore part? Are there any kind of punishment to failing or giving up a Siskur-Dah? Loss of renown, being chastised by their totem, or anything else?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26311-ulbrecht","name":"Ulbrecht","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26311_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-02T07:43:06-07:00","id":1535066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ulbrecht</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1534479-compatibility-between-1ed-and-2ed?p=1535050#post1535050\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what about the lore part? Are there any kind of punishment to failing or giving up a Siskur-Dah? Loss of renown, being chastised by their totem, or anything else?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing concretely enshrined, but from a sheer logistics perspective folks (particularly goal-oriented people like werewolves on the hunt) are likely to be put off by wasted time and abandoned tasks.<br /> <br /> Given the way the Primal Urge-based timer progresses and the way the Condition works, the general arc of a werewolf who has to get particularly strong is incentivized to do a lot of hunting in the Shadow and either get good at figuring out suitable prey or be very unchoosy about what they hunt to keep from being drawn towards the Flesh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}